#Requires -Version 7.2

# Ansi.Emoji.psm1
# Internal: the emoji table behind :name: tokens. Not public; Ansi.Core imports it,
# and ConvertFrom-AnsiMarkdown is the only caller.
#
# The names are the shortcodes emoji are commonly written with — the same
# :grinning_face: spelling other terminal libraries and chat clients take — so a
# token copied from elsewhere renders here. Every emoji Unicode gives a single
# codepoint sequence is in, 1430 of them; sequences that join several emoji into one
# (families, flags) are not.
#
# The table is data, not code: one line per emoji, its name and
# then its Unicode codepoints in hex. Codepoints rather than the glyphs themselves
# keep this file diffable in any editor, and the table is built on first lookup
# rather than at import, so a script that writes no emoji pays nothing for it.

